        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-08T10:46:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you\u0027re right, we may have corner cases if this says false, because networks that don\u0027t actually require validation end up with the VALIDATED flag. That means it\u0027s possible we think the offer can\u0027t beat the existing network, so we don\u0027t send the request to that provider.\n\nMaybe this should just say true in all cases ! If validation is possible, then this should be true (or the offer may lose to existing validated networks). If validation is not possible... then this should be true too, because then it competes against validated networks.",
